 "title": "Verticillium dahliae Pathogenicity and Protein Expression",
 "summary": "This cluster focuses on the pathogenic fungus Verticillium dahliae and its interactions with cotton. The fungus causes disease in cotton and regulates the development of the VdMFS2 gene. VdMFS2 is expressed in cotton and is a host for the fungus Vd592. The fungus also has pathogenicity towards Vd592. Additionally, VdMFS2 is silenced using the HIGS method. The cluster also includes various chemical and nutrient relations, such as the growth mediums for Vd592 and the nutrients it has. The fungus V. dahliae is also associated with the researcher Fradin EF.",
